hexagon: keep the fd map of an op batch correct after the buffer sort
Fold-into: patches/hexagon-host/0001-hexagon-host-timers-and-batch-cache.patch

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

sort_buffers puts the buffers of an op batch in the order of their size,
and it gives each tensor the new index of its buffer. It does not change
b_map, the map from the fd of a buffer to its index, which add_buffer
reads. A flush sorts the batch and then clears it, thus the map has no
effect there. The verify mode of the batch cache
(GGML_HEXAGON_BATCHCACHE=2) sorts the replayed batch to compare it with a
new packing, and the batch then gets the ops of the next split. Those ops
get the old index of a buffer from the map. The descriptor of such a
tensor then gives the offset of the tensor in a different buffer, and the
DSP reads or writes out of that buffer.

This patch writes the sorted index of each fd into the map at the end of
sort_buffers. A batch has a maximum of 16 buffers. The mode 1 of the batch
cache, which the app uses, does not sort a replay, thus the ops that the
app sends do not change.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
index bcd146d..f2e92d2 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
@@ -2681,6 +2681,13 @@ struct ggml_hexagon_opbatch {
         for (unsigned int i = 0; i < n_tens; i++) {
             h_tens[i].bi = remap[h_tens[i].bi];
         }
+
+        // add_buffer reads the index of a buffer from the fd map. The verify mode of the batch
+        // cache sorts a replay that gets more ops after the sort, thus the map must give the
+        // sorted indexes. O(n_bufs).
+        for (unsigned int i = 0; i < n_bufs; i++) {
+            b_map[(int) h_bufs[i].fd] = (int) i;
+        }
     }
 
     void update_mdev_group(uint32_t mdev_idx) {
